      "id": "ea78760d-d1a9-493e-b723-3b0ff24b94eb",
      "name": "DOC 1 - Workflow Details",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -144,
        -1104
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 794,
        "height": 1273,
        "content": "# Draft dental denial appeal packets from Gmail EOBs with OpenAI and Drive\n\n## What this workflow does\nThis workflow automates the operational process represented by **Draft dental denial appeal packets from Gmail EOBs with OpenAI and Drive** while keeping decisions, audit records, and notifications traceable.\n\n## Who it is for\nOperations teams, reviewers, and process owners configuring the connected services.\n\n## How it works\n1. **Receive Payer Denial Notice** — Starts the workflow when the configured gmailTrigger event occurs.\n2. **Normalize Denial Payload** — Normalizes, validates, or reshapes data for the next workflow step.\n3. **Extract Denial Line Items** — Applies the workflow's AI prompt or model to the current business record.\n4. **Denial Extraction Model** — Applies the workflow's AI prompt or model to the current business record.\n5. **Split Out Denied CPT Lines** — Controls routing, joining, batching, or approval state for this execution.\n6. **Score Appeal Strategy & Deadline** — Normalizes, validates, or reshapes data for the next workflow step.\n7. **Check Line Item Appealable** — Controls routing, joining, batching, or approval state for this execution.\n8. **Check Filing Deadline Urgency** — Controls routing, joining, batching, or approval state for this execution.\n9. **Tag Non-Appealable Reason** — Normalizes, validates, or reshapes data for the next workflow step.\n10. **Flag Priority Review** — Normalizes, validates, or reshapes data for the next workflow step.\n11. **Tag Standard Queue** — Normalizes, validates, or reshapes data for the next workflow step.\n12. **Log Non-Appealable Denial** — Reads or writes the operational record in the configured system of record.\n13. **Notify Billing Manager - Non-Appealable** — Sends the relevant decision, request, or exception to its recipient.\n14. **Merge Appealable Line Decisions** — Controls routing, joining, batching, or approval state for this execution.\n15. **Draft Appeal Letter** — Applies the workflow's AI prompt or model to the current business record.\n16. **Appeal Drafting Model** — Applies the workflow's AI prompt or model to the current business record.\n17. **Aggregate Appeal Packet Lines** — Normalizes, validates, or reshapes data for the next workflow step.\n18. **Shape Appeal Record** — Normalizes, validates, or reshapes data for the next workflow step.\n19. **Save Appeal Packet to Drive** — Reads or writes the operational record in the configured system of record.\n20. **Log Appeal Decision** — Reads or writes the operational record in the configured system of record.\n21. **Update Practice Management System** — Normalizes, validates, or reshapes data for the next workflow step.\n22. **Notify Front Desk of Drafted Appeal** — Sends the relevant decision, request, or exception to its recipient.\n\n## Expected result\nA routed, logged, and reviewable operational outcome using the configured integrations."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "76057367-9529-4d0e-bd94-747e79cc12ff",
      "name": "DOC 2 - Setup Guide",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
